      "excerpts": [
        {
          "start_line": 3,
          "start_column": 1,
          "text": "Modules make hgraph and extension capabilities available without exposing a\n"
        },
        {
          "start_line": 78,
          "start_column": 1,
          "text": "expression operator bindings come from the implicit hgraph prelude. Exported\n"
        },
        {
          "start_line": 98,
          "start_column": 1,
          "text": "The `hgraph.native` module provides `len` and `is_empty` for `str`,\n"
        },
        {
          "start_line": 101,
          "start_column": 1,
          "text": "Additional string and window queries live in parts of the same module; see\nthe [native inventory](https://github.com/hhenson/hgraph/blob/main/language/stdlib/hgl/hgraph/README.md). Value operations keep\n"
        },
        {
          "start_line": 107,
          "start_column": 1,
          "text": "use hgraph.native as native\n"
        },
        {
          "start_line": 116,
          "start_column": 1,
          "text": "The native library must be included in the package that runs the program.\nFor build configuration, see the\n[package-authoring guide](https://github.com/hhenson/hgraph/blob/main/language/docs/developer-guide/native-modules-and-packages.md#building-a-package).\nThe [module inventory](https://github.com/hhenson/hgraph/blob/main/language/stdlib/hgl/hgraph/README.md) lists available\nfunctions and current type restrictions.\n"
        }
